///
/// ═══ CORRECTED DIAGNOSIS (v-wasm-opt, 2026-07-16 — same root as the sibling repro; filed locus is WRONG) ═══
/// "recursion trips a select.rs float-compare misclassification" is a RED HERRING. Recursion just defeats
/// constant-folding so a genuine RUNTIME float compare survives to lowering. A BARE `def run(x: Float64,
/// y: Float64) = if x < y then 1 else 0` (no recursion, no compound) DECLINES identically. TRUE ROOT:
/// runtime float compare is UNIMPLEMENTED — `is_scalar` (lower.rs:20160) excludes Float, so `Core::Compare`
/// dispatch routes every runtime Float compare to the compound-heap-walk decline; no float-compare Prim/Lir/
/// emit exists. This is a CORE/NUMERIC gap gated on 2 spec decisions (canonical-byte `=` vs wasm f64.eq;
/// NaN ordering the const fold DECLINES). RE-FILE to numeric-model/core + design, NOT the wasm backend.
/// See the sibling repro's corrected-diagnosis block for the full detail.
